1
00:00:00,210 --> 00:00:01,960
Chapter four. After the election.

2
00:00:02,660 --> 00:00:07,801
September ninth, at Joint Base Andrews. "This war will end immediately after our election."

3
00:00:08,520 --> 00:00:11,362
That week, US oil crossed one hundred dollars again.

4
00:00:11,980 --> 00:00:16,142
Three days later, in Ireland. "I think it'll be right after the midterms, actually."

5
00:00:16,820 --> 00:00:19,523
"And oil will come tumbling down when that happens."

6
00:00:20,180 --> 00:00:26,904
October second, at a rally in Mobile, Alabama. "It's going to end very soon, and probably right after the midterms."

7
00:00:27,520 --> 00:00:30,924
October eighth, on Truth Social. The blockade stays.

8
00:00:31,510 --> 00:00:35,585
But "we will not be attacking Iran at any time prior to the Midterm Elections."

9
00:00:36,300 --> 00:00:40,005
October ninth. "One way or another, it's gonna be over soon."

10
00:00:40,760 --> 00:00:43,646
October thirtieth. "It's going to get wrapped up soon."

11
00:00:44,340 --> 00:00:49,647
November first. Before a rally in Iowa. "We'll put it away very soon, one way or the other."

12
00:00:50,260 --> 00:00:54,490
On stage that night. "It's going to be over very soon. Very soon."

13
00:00:55,140 --> 00:00:58,548
And. "At some point, we're going to have to give them the hammer."

14
00:00:59,230 --> 00:01:04,669
By the end of October, the Pentagon counted twenty-three American service members killed in the war.

15
00:01:05,360 --> 00:01:08,709
Oil was up about seventy percent from a year earlier.
